        "original_id": "d92077c4-a937-5392-bd94-f66a45917923",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dan McCafferty, Eddie Vedder, Billy Rankin\n- Bands: Nazareth, Pearl Jam\n- Albums: Rock 'n' Roll Telephone\n- Roles: vocalists, guitarist, singer-songwriter\n\nFacts:\n- Dan McCafferty was born on 14 October 1946 in Dunfermline, Scotland.\n- Dan McCafferty is a Scottish vocalist best known as the lead singer of Nazareth from the band's founding in 1968 until his retirement from touring in 2013.\n- Billy Rankin is best known for his work with Nazareth from 1980 to 1983 and again from 1990 to 1994.\n- Billy Rankin also had a successful solo career that included the US hit single \"Baby Come Back.\"\n- Eddie Vedder was born Edward Louis Severson on December 23, 1964.\n- Eddie Vedder is an American musician, singer, and songwriter best known as a member of Pearl Jam, where he performs lead vocals and is one of three guitarists.\n- Rock 'n' Roll Telephone was the last Nazareth album with original singer Dan McCafferty, who left the group before the album's release.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "063e3ebc-ab75-5813-8d42-12b205c1a878",
        "text": "Page: Dan McCafferty. Sentence: William Daniel \"Dan\" McCafferty (born 14 October 1946, Dunfermline, Scotland) is a Scottish vocalist, best known as the lead singer for the Scottish hard rock band Nazareth from its founding in 1968 to his retirement from touring with the band in 2013.\nPage: Eddie Vedder. Sentence: Eddie Vedder (born Edward Louis Severson; December 23, 1964) is an American musician, singer and songwriter best known as a member of the rock band Pearl Jam, with whom he performs lead vocals and is one of three guitarists.\nPage: Rock 'n' Roll Telephone. Sentence: It is their last album with original singer Dan McCafferty who left the group before its release.\nPage: Billy Rankin (guitarist). Sentence: Best known for his work with Nazareth (1980–83 & 1990–94), he also had a successful solo career, including a US hit single \"Baby Come Back\".",
